'''''Parapholis filiformis''''' is a species of annual herb in the family [[Poaceae]] (true grasses). They have a self-supporting growth form and simple, broad leaves. Individuals can grow to 0.17 m.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Parapholis filiformis (Roth) C.E.Hubb. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/1115439|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mifsud |first=Stephen |date=2002-08-23 |title=Parapholis filiformis (Hard-Grass) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands. |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/POAC/Parapholis_filiformis.php |access-date=2022-03-07 |website=www.maltawildplants.com |language=en-us}}</ref>

